{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed: Gerrit change 3421, merged as 07f023db8031f1a09b5d0e51ea1ca3ff35cd63c2 (patch set 2, LLM-Review +1, Verified +1). make verify exited 0 on the pushed tree (21390 + 226 passed).\n\nImplementation note against Approach step 1-2: the helper is `_gated(solve, *, repo_root)` in `src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py`, which resolves the SOURCE_LOCAL handle once (before any case) and enters `gate_source.gate_read_root(handle)` around each `solve` call, rather than a context manager around the loop. Same session, same explicit source; per-call wrapping also covers default-solver construction without re-indenting the loops. Applied in both `run_eval` and `calibrate_criterion`.\n\nAC evidence: tests `test_run_eval_opens_a_gate_session_for_its_solver`, `test_calibrate_criterion_opens_a_gate_session_for_its_solver` (uses the `necessity` criterion, see militant-vixenish-gorilla), `test_run_eval_reports_an_all_errored_epoch_as_a_run_failure`; all 3 fail against origin/main 05c6414358f code."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794984382585307672,"uuid":"93c6a86c-2fae-48b5-8f16-5eccecafc738"}